WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.862
Unit 1 is who does what.

2
00:00:01.862 --> 00:00:07.202
The agency's system access management tool
is the request front end: an owner asks

3
00:00:07.202 --> 00:00:12.301
for, changes or retires an account there,
and it hands the request to SailPoint.

4
00:00:12.301 --> 00:00:15.450
It never approves or
writes anything itself.

5
00:00:15.450 --> 00:00:21.067
SailPoint approves every request, whatever
its risk tier, aggregates the accounts,

6
00:00:21.067 --> 00:00:25.300
correlates each one to its owners
and runs the certifications.

7
00:00:25.300 --> 00:00:29.250
It never writes a G M S
A in Active Directory.

8
00:00:29.250 --> 00:00:33.152
ServiceNow holds the change
record, the typed findings and

9
00:00:33.152 --> 00:00:36.975
the decommission ticket, and
closes a task only on a re-read.

10
00:00:36.975 --> 00:00:38.787
It never approves the account.

11
00:00:38.787 --> 00:00:44.257
The pipeline runs Chapter 6's approved
plan as G M S A dash M S A pipe,

12
00:00:44.257 --> 00:00:47.663
with only the delegated rights it needs.

13
00:00:47.663 --> 00:00:53.388
And a person still runs the D M S A
steps, the uninstall and every delete.

14
00:00:53.388 --> 00:00:56.721
The pipeline's identity
is itself a G M S A,

15
00:00:56.721 --> 00:01:01.130
with two owners, a sponsor
and its own certification.
